  "note": "Baseline snapshot of every claim ID already in play at this commit — the line between 'existing' and 'newly introduced' for the claimlint C14 BARE-IDS naming-convention check (operator ruling 2026-08-22, fable-absorption-gaps-2026-08-22.md §6.3(2)). Drawn as a SNAPSHOT, not a date heuristic: a findings file's `date` field is author-supplied and unverifiable, and a git-blame heuristic would re-classify an ID every time its line moved. Sources unioned: register rows (docs/epistemic/CLAIMS.md), archived rows (archives/register/INDEX.md), every claims[].id and new_rows[].id in findings/*.json, and every rejections.json claim_id. Rationale for including the last three and not just the register: an ID that a findings file already proposed is already cited in the tree, and the operator's ruling is explicit that existing IDs are NOT mass-renamed because the citations are the evidence. Malformed IDs (prose appended after the identifier) are recorded VERBATIM so they match on lookup; C14 does not launder them. This file is APPEND-ONLY in spirit: removing an ID from it retroactively makes an old ID new and would flag settled history.",
